Hunks of the shared Metal series that this engine's older ggml cannot take verbatim.

Everything else in patches/llama/metal/0001-* applies here unchanged, so improvements to the
shared backend reach the image engine on their own. These four need a hand:

  - dequantize_q4_1: upstream rewrote the function around us
  - the sum_rows shared-memory size, which must follow the card's real SIMD width
  - the wave64 entries of supports_op, whose switch is shaped differently here
  - the ggml_metal_init call site, which gains the prefetch argument

build-engines.sh applies the shared series with --reject, checks the rejected hunks are
exactly the four files below, and then applies this patch. If that set ever changes the build
stops, so this engine cannot silently end up with a hunk missing.

